WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.113 --> 00:00:01.483
How long have you been in a cult?

00:00:01.483 --> 00:00:03.109
What's it like to be a Chia human?

00:00:03.109 --> 00:00:05.605
You look like you could
stick your finger in a socket

00:00:05.605 --> 00:00:07.660
without having stuck
your finger in a socket.

00:00:07.660 --> 00:00:10.243
(upbeat music)

00:00:12.954 --> 00:00:15.114
I volunteered to let a comedian heckle me

00:00:15.114 --> 00:00:16.182
all day tomorrow.

00:00:16.182 --> 00:00:17.087
He's gonna come to my house.

00:00:17.087 --> 00:00:18.224
He's gonna wake me up.

00:00:18.224 --> 00:00:19.385
He's gonna spend all day with me.

00:00:19.385 --> 00:00:21.568
I'm kinda looking forward
to it 'cause I like company,

00:00:21.568 --> 00:00:24.371
but I also feel like it
might get really annoying,

00:00:24.371 --> 00:00:25.686
especially if his jokes are bad.

00:00:25.686 --> 00:00:27.670
My name is J. Chris Newberg
and I've been a comedian

00:00:27.670 --> 00:00:29.098
for 18 years.

00:00:29.098 --> 00:00:31.733
Throughout my career, I've
been heckled from time to time,

00:00:31.733 --> 00:00:33.893
but I've never had the joy and pleasure

00:00:33.893 --> 00:00:35.599
of heckling someone back.

00:00:35.599 --> 00:00:38.026
I volunteered to do this
because I think I have really

00:00:38.026 --> 00:00:40.522
thick skin and I like good comedy.

00:00:40.522 --> 00:00:43.113
I imagine he'll just be
like, observing what I do

00:00:43.113 --> 00:00:44.158
and making fun of it.

00:00:44.158 --> 00:00:46.039
I can't imagine it could
get that personal because

00:00:46.039 --> 00:00:47.490
how would he know anything about me?

00:00:47.490 --> 00:00:48.617
I've never met this guy.

00:00:48.617 --> 00:00:50.904
I've done some extensive
research on Jordan.

00:00:50.904 --> 00:00:53.330
I've looked online at his
Facebook and Instagram

00:00:53.330 --> 00:00:54.735
and Twitter profiles.

00:00:54.735 --> 00:00:56.070
I've talked to his friends.

00:00:56.070 --> 00:00:57.684
I've talked to his coworkers.

00:00:57.684 --> 00:00:59.507
I've talked to his ex-girlfriend.

00:00:59.507 --> 00:01:00.343
I'm comin' at him.

00:01:00.343 --> 00:01:02.165
I'm not really sure how I'm going to feel,

00:01:02.165 --> 00:01:04.557
'cause I hate everything
hecklers represent.

00:01:04.557 --> 00:01:05.590
I'm gonna try to be mean,

00:01:05.590 --> 00:01:07.254
but I'm not a mean person.

00:01:07.254 --> 00:01:08.301
But, fuck him.

00:01:08.301 --> 00:01:10.425
It's 7:53 in the morning.

00:01:10.425 --> 00:01:11.923
I found Jordan's place.

00:01:11.923 --> 00:01:13.130
I'm with Kelly.

00:01:13.130 --> 00:01:14.732
She's a producer at Buzzfeed.

00:01:14.732 --> 00:01:16.218
She's gonna be followin' me.

00:01:16.218 --> 00:01:17.751
We're outside

00:01:17.751 --> 00:01:18.918
his apartment.

00:01:20.142 --> 00:01:22.964
It's pretty good so far.

00:01:22.964 --> 00:01:24.949
It's uh, pretty dirty.

00:01:24.949 --> 00:01:28.780
I don't understand the
science of this decor.

00:01:28.780 --> 00:01:31.369
Like, what girl doesn't come in here,

00:01:31.369 --> 00:01:32.995
see this,

00:01:32.995 --> 00:01:36.129
and then just leap right off the balcony?

00:01:36.129 --> 00:01:38.208
Here's Jordan killing it,

00:01:38.208 --> 00:01:40.750
from when he played a young Carrot Top.

00:01:40.750 --> 00:01:43.078
I wonder which one of those
socks are his girlfriend.

00:01:43.078 --> 00:01:44.018
- [Jordan] Hello.

00:01:44.018 --> 00:01:45.516
Hey buddy.

00:01:45.516 --> 00:01:48.409
(laughs) Super excited to be here

00:01:48.409 --> 00:01:51.857
with the third baseman of
the Los Angeles Dodgers.

00:01:51.857 --> 00:01:53.601
Dude, I don't even know
who the third baseman is

00:01:53.601 --> 00:01:54.687
of the Los Angeles Dodgers.

00:01:54.687 --> 00:01:55.848
Look in the mirror, buddy.

00:01:55.848 --> 00:01:58.611
So, what's it like to be
the body double for sadness?

00:01:58.611 --> 00:02:00.945
People do say I have resting sad face.

00:02:00.945 --> 00:02:03.058
So, I heard you and your
girlfriend just broke up.

00:02:03.058 --> 00:02:04.950
True.
Good for her.

00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:06.564
Damn, getting some--

00:02:06.564 --> 00:02:08.166
Gettin' deep.
Yeah, and you're

00:02:08.166 --> 00:02:10.407
putting on your girlfriends.
What?

00:02:10.407 --> 00:02:11.579
You'll understand later.

00:02:11.579 --> 00:02:14.235
How long have you played
bass for Mumford and Sons?

00:02:14.235 --> 00:02:17.207
You're flossing on the day that
you're going to the dentist.

00:02:17.207 --> 00:02:19.250
Isn't that like cleaning
your house before you have

00:02:19.250 --> 00:02:20.620
a cleaning lady come over?

00:02:20.620 --> 00:02:24.382
Which, obviously, has never happened.

00:02:24.382 --> 00:02:25.868
So, you're putting product in right now?

00:02:25.868 --> 00:02:27.331
Mmhmm.
That's cool.

00:02:27.331 --> 00:02:29.026
How long have you been a before model?

00:02:29.026 --> 00:02:31.804
You're like the most handsome
of all the Keebler elves.

00:02:31.804 --> 00:02:33.182
We're going to the dentist.

00:02:33.182 --> 00:02:34.102
You're gonna let him drill ya?

00:02:34.102 --> 00:02:35.182
Well, hopefully not.
(playful music)

00:02:35.182 --> 00:02:36.536
Hopefully, I won't need any drillings.

00:02:36.536 --> 00:02:37.837
Maybe just some poking.

00:02:37.837 --> 00:02:39.685
Minimal poking, hopefully.

00:02:39.685 --> 00:02:40.518
That's cool.

00:02:40.518 --> 00:02:41.763
That was my nickname in high school.

00:02:41.763 --> 00:02:43.400
Do you find that you're
on Tinder most of the time

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:44.643
during sex?

00:02:44.643 --> 00:02:45.978
What are your favorite dating apps?

00:02:45.978 --> 00:02:47.441
Tinder is the tried and true.

00:02:47.441 --> 00:02:49.554
What's your opening
line usually, on Tinder?

00:02:49.554 --> 00:02:50.912
I don't use repeat opening lines

00:02:50.912 --> 00:02:52.270
'cause I think that's insincere.

00:02:52.270 --> 00:02:54.848
I use their profiles to
come up with opening lines.

00:02:54.848 --> 00:02:57.158
What was your favorite
that you've ever used?

00:02:57.158 --> 00:02:59.329
Oh man, I had a really good one recently.

00:02:59.329 --> 00:03:01.825
It didn't get a response
and I was bummed about it.

00:03:01.825 --> 00:03:06.713
Her profile just said I like
people, places, and things.

00:03:06.713 --> 00:03:08.965
And, I said, what you
got against adjectives?

00:03:08.965 --> 00:03:12.715
They probably have very nice
things to say about you.

00:03:12.715 --> 00:03:14.480
I thought that was pretty good.

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:16.361
It's weird that that
didn't get a response.

00:03:16.361 --> 00:03:18.265
So, do you still talk to Harry Potter?

00:03:18.265 --> 00:03:19.763
Do you get sad when some
of your personalities

00:03:19.763 --> 00:03:21.017
